## Third-party components

Third-party packages, model weights, datasets, container images, and services
are not relicensed by this notice. Preserve their original notices and check
their terms before redistributing them. Components with noteworthy conditions:

- pypdfium2 (Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause) bundles Google PDFium.
- The optional document OCR path invokes Tesseract OCR with vie/eng
  traineddata (Apache-2.0); it is disabled by default.
- fastembed (Apache-2.0) embeds ONNX Runtime (MIT) and is used with the
  MIT-licensed bge-m3 embedding weights.
- Qdrant (Apache-2.0) serves dense, sparse (bm25), and hybrid retrieval.
- Kuzu (MIT) stores the knowledge graph.
- Redis is pinned to 7.2.x (BSD-3-Clause) on purpose: Redis 7.4+ is
  RSALv2/SSPL, which is not an OSI-approved license.
- Infrastructure services: PostgreSQL (PostgreSQL License), RabbitMQ
  (MPL-2.0), SeaweedFS (Apache-2.0), Keycloak and APISIX (Apache-2.0).
- The optional observability profile runs Grafana (AGPL-3.0) as an unmodified
  standalone service accessed over the network; no Grafana code is linked
  into OpenVie.
- Mozilla PDF.js (npm package `pdfjs-dist`, declared in `frontend/package.json`,
  Apache License, Version 2.0). Its web worker (`pdf.worker.min.mjs`) is not
  committed to this repository: it is copied from the installed `pdfjs-dist`
  package into `frontend/public/` at build/run time by
  `frontend/scripts/prepare-pdf-worker.mjs`, so the shipped artifact always
  matches the declared dependency version. `CHANGELOG.md` previously recorded
  a vendored copy; that has been removed in v1.0.0.
- sharp (frontend runtime dependency, Apache-2.0) bundles prebuilt libvips
  binaries licensed under LGPL-3.0-or-later; Next.js image optimization utilizes
  it dynamically.
- H2 Database (com.h2database:h2, MPL-2.0 / EPL-1.0) is present only in test
  scope for in-memory integration testing and is never packaged into production JARs.
- Eclipse Paho MQTT client (org.eclipse.paho:org.eclipse.paho.client.mqttv3)
  is dual-licensed EPL-2.0 / EDL-1.0 (BSD-3-Clause); OpenVie uses it unmodified
  under the BSD-3-Clause terms for MQTT connector jobs.
- AI model weights referenced in configuration (such as vylinh, bge-m3, or
  models configured for AI manifest drafting) are third-party models with their
  own upstream licenses and are not relicensed by OpenVie.
- Remaining Python, Java, and frontend dependencies are permissive
  (Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, 0BSD, or CDDL-1.1/MPL-2.0
  where unmodified) and listed in `rag-chatbot-fastapi/pyproject.toml`,
  `api/pom.xml`, and `frontend/package.json`.
